[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107691,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Peritoneal inclusion cysts are benign cysts lined by mesothelium.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107692,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9055/0 Peritoneal inclusion cysts</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107693,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>DC51.Y &amp; XH8U12 Other specified disorders of peritoneum or retroperitoneum &amp; Peritoneal inclusion cysts</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107694,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> multilocular peritoneal inclusion cysts.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> benign cystic mesothelioma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107695,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107696,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Peritoneum, spleen, liver, and testis {17535091; 23725510}</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107697,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Peritoneal inclusion cysts can be detected incidentally or manifest with abdominal or pelvic pain, abdominal distension, or as an inguinal hernia {29511797; 20620295}. One patient who presented with pelvic pain passed the lesion in the form of string-like material through her cervix {19433156}. A rare case has been associated with ascites {7528798}. Occasionally, this lesion is seen in patients with renal developmental anomalies {23084231}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107698,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Peritoneal inclusion cysts are uncommon. They have a slight female predilection and are seen from the gestational period to the age of 19&nbsp;years {17535091; 17598115; 29511797}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107699,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although some lesions are congenital and others are reactive (i.e. secondary to abdominal/pelvic surgery, inflammation, or bleeding) {17535091; 17598115; 25143853}, in many cases no etiological factor is identified {19232301; 26524665}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107700,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FISH shows no <em>CDKN2A</em> (<em>P16</em>) deletion {26288396}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107701,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are single or multiple cysts, which can be unilocular or multilocular and range in size from a few millimetres to 400&nbsp;mm {19386139; 29511797; 3174512}. Their inner and outer surfaces are usually smooth, and some cases can have a pedicle {19232301}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107702,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Peritoneal inclusion cysts are lined by a single layer of bland, flat or cuboidal mesothelial cells. Metaplastic or reactive changes, hobnail cells, and adenomatoid areas can be seen. The septa are composed of fibroconnective tissue without smooth muscle bundles. There is no invasion into the adjacent tissue. Calretinin and CK5/6 are expressed, and PAX8, ER, and PR are variably positive {29511797; 28877056; 29241740; 12733118}. BAP1 expression is retained.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107703,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytology shows bland or reactive mesothelial cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107704,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107705,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> cyst(s) lined by bland mesothelial cells, with no invasion into adjacent tissue.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> positive staining for mesothelial markers.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107706,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107707,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 274,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Peritoneal inclusion cysts are benign. Recurrences are seen infrequently {19232301; 23084231}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T14:23:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]